    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="1079" n="1039" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1039"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">783.00/9–2552: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 506<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in
                        Syria</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d506-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-10-24T17:57:00-05:00">October 24, 1952—5:57
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>265. Urdes 185 Sept 25 contains valuable info re possible Shishikli conditions
                    for settlement of certain problems with Israel. Question arises as to how to
                    utilize these suggestions. Israelis continually complain, with some
                    justification, that Syrs unwilling even discuss any of problems contained in
                        refdes. (Example: Syr postponements and
                    restricted instructions Oct 9 mtg.) Dept therefore desires know under what
                    conditions Syrs will discuss these problems. Also, can Dept make known Syr terms
                    to Israel Gov without of course revealing source? Such an approach wld be made
                    to ascertain whether or not possibility for negotiated <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >modus vivendi</hi> between Syr and Israel exists.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Bruce</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d506-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d506-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Tel Aviv.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
